ounts aggregate across all aliases\n    71→\n    72→4. **Missing aliases for Prince Prospero**\n    73→   - Problem: \"the duke\" is used in the text but not captured as alias\n    74→   - Evidence: \"as might have been expected from the duke's love of the bizarre\"\n    75→   - Location: Alias detection\n    76→\n    77→### MEDIUM\n    78→5. **Canonical name format includes leading article**\n    79→   - Problem: Character name is \"the Prince Prospero\" instead of \"Prince Prospero\"\n    80→   - Location: Character name normalization\n    81→\n    82→6. **Too many common words in pronunciation guide (65 in \"Other\")**\n    83→   - Problem: Common words like \"dauntless\", \"chiming\", \"magnificence\" are flagged\n    84→   - Location: Pronunciation flagging threshold\n    85→\n    86→7. **Foreign word false positive: \"decorum\"**\n    87→   - Problem: \"decorum\" flagged as foreign word - it's standard English (Latin-derived)\n    88→   - Location: Foreign word detection\n    89→\n    90→### LOW\n    91→8. **Timing table formatting issues**\n    92→   - Problem: \"started_at\" and \"ended_at\" rows show empty duration values\n    93→   - Location: HTML template\n    94→\n    95→## Fix History\n    96→\n    97→### Attempt 1 Fixes Applied\n    98→1. **Cross-group epithet resolution** (consensus.py) - Did not produce expected results\n    99→2. **Article filtering for pronunciation** (cmu_proposer.py) - Partially worked (\"the\" removed)\n   100→\n   101→### Attempt 2 Fixes Applied\n   102→1. **Proper name with article classification** (consensus.py:_is_descriptive_handle())\n   103→   - Partially worked: Profile now generated, mention count improved 3→6\n   104→   - Caused regression: \"the mummer\" incorrectly merged with Prince Prospero\n   105→\n   106→### Attempt 3 Fixes Applied\n   107→1. **Enhanced cross-group resolution with conflict detection** (consensus.py:CROSS_GROUP_SYSTEM, CROSS_GROUP_PROMPT, _llm_cross_group_resolution())\n   108→   - Root cause: s